{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag a standards issue before we finalize. Per the network's current standards memo — which was issued after the draft voting rules were circulated — there are three binding requirements that the current draft does not yet reflect: voters must be at least 13 years old, each voter may cast exactly one vote per verified account, and voting must close at 9:50 PM Eastern. The draft as it stands doesn't specify an age floor, a one-vote-per-verified-account limit, or a 9:50 PM close. These need to be incorporated into the final package."}
```

